-- title:
--   Characters of Γ₀(N) over ℤ[1/q] factor through (ℤ/N)^×
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $N$ a natural number coprime to $q$. Write $\mathbb{Z}[1/q]$ for the localisation [`Ihara.ZAway q`](def/Gamma0Away.html#L11) of $\mathbb{Z}$ away from $q$, and let [`Ihara.Gamma0Away N q`](def/Gamma0Away.html#L15) be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[1/q])$ consisting of those $g$ whose lower left entry $g_{1,0}$ is divisible by the image of $N$ in $\mathbb{Z}[1/q]$. Let $A$ be an additive abelian group satisfying two torsion conditions: $a+a=0$ implies $a=0$, and $a+a+a=0$ implies $a=0$; thus $A$ has no $2$- or $3$-torsion. Let $\Psi$ be a group homomorphism from [`Ihara.Gamma0Away N q`](def/Gamma0Away.html#L15) to the multiplicative copy `Multiplicative A` of $A$. The assertion is that there exists a homomorphism $\chi : (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times \to$ `Multiplicative A` with $\Psi = \chi \circ$ [`Ihara.gamma0AwayUnitsChar N q hqN`](def/Gamma0AwayUnitsChar.html#L51), where the latter is the character sending $g$ to the unit determined by the image of the lower right entry $g_{1,1}$ under the reduction map [`Ihara.zAwayToZMod N q hqN`](def/Gamma0AwayUnitsChar.html#L19) from $\mathbb{Z}[1/q]$ to $\mathbb{Z}/N$ (i.e. $\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix} \mapsto d \bmod N$, which lies in $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$). Equality of homomorphisms is asserted on the nose, not merely up to the subgroup generated by torsion.
--
--   This is the form, for the localised group $\Gamma_0(N)(\mathbb{Z}[1/q])$, of the statement that modulo $2$- and $3$-torsion phenomena the abelianisation of $\Gamma_0(N)(\mathbb{Z}[1/q])$ is a quotient of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ via $d \bmod N$; it rests on the congruence subgroup property for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[1/q])$ in Mennicke's form. It is used to obtain the finiteness of the abelianisation of $\Gamma_0(N)(\mathbb{Z}[1/q])$ ([`Ihara.finite_abelianization_gamma0Away`](thm.html#Ihara.finite_abelianization_gamma0Away)) and, through the amalgam decomposition $\Gamma_0(N)(\mathbb{Z}[1/q]) \cong \Gamma_0(N) *_{\Gamma_0(Nq)} \Gamma_0(N)$, the factorisation statement over $\Gamma_0(N)$ used in Ihara's lemma ([`Ihara.ihara_hom_factor`](thm.html#Ihara.ihara_hom_factor)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ihara_gamma0Away_hom_factor.lean

import Definitions.Def_Gamma0AwayUnitsChar

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem Ihara.gamma0Away_hom_factor {N q : ℕ} (hq : q.Prime) (hqN : N.Coprime q)
    {A : Type*} [AddCommGroup A]
    (h2 : ∀ a : A, a + a = 0 → a = 0) (h3 : ∀ a : A, a + a + a = 0 → a = 0)
    (Ψ : Gamma0Away N q →* Multiplicative A) :
    ∃ χ : (ZMod N)ˣ →* Multiplicative A, Ψ = χ.comp (gamma0AwayUnitsChar N q hqN) := by sorry
